A||N||40||Elenor84||Transmission help.  I have no 2nd gear...every other one works but that one...||||1||
Z||000000||Elenor84||05-23-2001||05:39 PM||||Hey guys...I was at a movie the other day and wen I left I started going in first then wen I shifted to second I felt a jerk and then nothing...I have  no second gear...third and 4rth work fine...I have a 4 speed trany on a 2.5 litre...I need help fast cause this is my daily driver...thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||ROB MAC||05-23-2001||05:52 PM||||I had trouble with 3rd which turned out to be a cable adjustment. Haynes Manual tells how to do the adjustment. If not cable or linkage ,must be internal. Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||05-23-2001||06:06 PM||||Alright well I have the hanes manual but is the ajustment underneithe or interior? of the car...<BR>or did u drop the tranny?  thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierowrecker||05-23-2001||09:50 PM||||It is adjusted at the trans in the engine compartment...<BR>You need to expose the shifter pivot pin also...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||05-23-2001||10:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Elenor84:<BR><B>...is the ajustment underneath or interior? of the car...<BR>or did u drop the tranny?  thx!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You do not have to crawl under the car to adjust the shift linkage.  You do not have to drop the transmission to adjust the linkage, either.<P>I would suggest that you have someone sit in the car and operate the shifter while you watch what happens at the other ends of the cables on top of the trans.  Have your assistant shift into 2nd; notice the way the shift shaft is trying to rotate.  If you can rotate the shift shaft a little farther, it should click into 2nd.<P>Loosen the big nut on the cable end, rotate the shift shaft until it clicks into 2nd.  Then retighten the bug nut.  Next, verify that it will shift into all of the gears.  You're done - until you have time (like a weekend) to properly adjust it per the procedure in the manual.<P>BTW, if the big nut on the cable end is found loose already, that's a good indication that you've found the problem.  <P>If it clicks into 2nd, but you still have "no go," then you have internal problems.  But that would mean more downtime, so for now let's say it's the linkage  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">       ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Elenor84||05-24-2001||12:27 AM||||Alright I just tryed what u said and it didn't work...I loosened the bolt and but it into second then retightend it...it is going into second...and I'm hearing a click in the tranny...so I take it this isn't good...how internal do u think it is?  It just doesen't seem likly because its only my second gear u know?...any more idea's...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Elenor84||05-24-2001||12:28 AM||||and also what is the shifter pivot pin? thx<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||ROB MAC||05-24-2001||01:23 PM||||The proper adjustment is to remove the shifter console cover and place pins or drill bits in guide holes on the shifter in 1st gear. Then you adjust the cables at the linkage end as per the Haynes book . Don't be scared cuz it ain't hard. I also had a lot of play in the linkage which I removed some of with washers ( as an experiment ) . Shifting is smoother than ever. Also my reverse lights now stay on ! Also check to see if the black plastic outer sleeve on the shift cables ( at the tranny ) is broken causing binding.||||reg||1
Z||000008||ROB MAC||05-24-2001||01:30 PM||||That metallic thunk when the gear is selected is normal.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Elenor84||05-24-2001||05:05 PM||||Ok I have ripped my interior to peices...now I do have the hanes manual so I will try the ajustment in the interior...I'll get back to u...if the clunk is normal then what is wrong?  Internal...its getting to the point were I'm thinking of putting a new tranny in...hwo much is an izuzu 5 speed?<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Elenor84||05-24-2001||05:56 PM||||O crap!  I just fu@#ed up my linkage....first gear is now reverse...someone please help!!!!!  this is killing me to see my car like this...I've been reading my hanes manual...it says to put the pins in the alignment holes...now were are they??????????  the interior is off and I'm looking down at the shifter and cables..were are the alignment holes?  thx!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||ROB MAC||05-25-2001||10:22 AM||||AT the front of the shifter when you put it in first , a hole in the shifter will line up with a hole in the base and you can put a 5/32 drill bit in. The other goes in sideways from driver side. When they are in place then you adjust the cables in the order as described. Look at the photos , the arrows point to the holes.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Elenor84||05-25-2001||05:38 PM||||k I'll go try that...I'll get back to u...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000013||EdsB52||05-25-2001||06:25 PM||||What are ya bitchin' bout? In my day we only had 2 speed transmissions, here ya got 4, you lose 1, you still have 3. Myaaaa, in my day we had two gears, and we liked it!<P>Too bad you're in Canada 'cause I have two boat anchors (4 speed transmissions) in great condition that I'de give ya to haul away. I even have a clutch assy with a couple thousand miles on that I'de give ya for next to nothing. Good luck, Ed.||||reg||1
