Z||000015||Elenor84||05-26-2001||05:49 AM||||Alittle more info?  Tell me about your experience...broken teeth?<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Elenor84||05-26-2001||07:16 PM||||Alright guys I really need your help!!!  Here is the total situation in full.  My interior is all out so I can see in the shifter place.  I put in a drill bit in the alignment holes on the shifter and then I did the linkage.  Now it is even worse...1st gear is now reverse...it won't even go into second or reverse and 3rd gear is my first gear and now forth doesen't work so I take it its second...what is going on?  I need help...I don't have very much money just to put it into a shop and tell them to go nuts...whats goin on and what do u guys suggest I do?  Thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000017||StuGood||05-26-2001||10:42 PM||||Sounds as if at this point, the "select" cable is slipping or out of adjustment, so that you effectively cannot get the thing to respond properly to the side-to-side movements of the shifter.  Does that sound right to you?  If so...<P>Point 1: Make sure that both ends of the select cable housing (sheath) are anchored (to a bracket, at each end).  The front end of the cable's housing should be anchored to the car;  the aft end of the cable's housing should be fixed to the transmission case.  Is it possible that a clip fell off the end of the cable housing, allowing the housing (sheath) to move-?<P>Point 2:  I believe the side-to-side motions of the shifter are supposed to result in the shift shaft being moved in and out of the transmission.  There should be essentially no slop in the cables and/or levers that accomplish this.  The levers are on top of the transmission case - check to see if perhaps a pivot pin fell out, allowing one of the levers to flop around.<P>Point 3) The fore-and-aft motions of the shifter are supposed to result in a twisting of the shift shaft.  That motion is carried by the "shift" cable.    <P>Since it worked (sort of) before, I believe it will be possible to adjust the linkage (cables) so that you'll be back to where you were before - in other words, to where you can shift into all gears including 2nd.  Even if 2nd gear is dead, at least the car will be driveable that way.  <P>Try not to panic - with a little patience, you should be able get it working well enough to get by.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Elenor84||05-26-2001||10:54 PM||||Your # 1 and 2 options sound right...the thing ontop of the trany with the cables: the second metal peice barely moves...side to side moviement...I think thats my problem...I was screwing around with it thoguh...I will go check that out and get back to u...thank you very mcuh<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Elenor84||05-29-2001||05:36 PM||||Alright...I have 1 more thing to throw in here...wen I first started looking at my linkage before I screwed it up the second shift shaft(bottom one/smaller one) moved around wen I shifted from first to second...is that right?  If not then that might be my problem...because now it is extremly hard to move it up and down...I'll go take a look and get back to u but do u think that I might just need to replace that cable?...thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000020||ROB MAC||05-29-2001||06:08 PM||||It does not take much to throw it out of whack. Be sure it is in 1st with both drill bits in place. Remove the play in the cable on the right like the book says by pushing the linkage and tightening the nut at the same time. Then do the same to the other. ||||reg||1
Z||000021||EdsB52||05-29-2001||08:02 PM||||If you need a tranny, I'll ship you a 4 speed for the cost of shipping. A lot of guys like 'em, but I think the ratios suck. I burned out a good 4 cyl motor 'cause I had to wind it up to 4 grand to get any speed out of the f'n thing. I have another one that has &lt;100,000 that I drove for just a few miles before I totalled it, that is in great shape and has been sitting for 6 years. I probably even have cables and a shifter. It will cost ya a few bucks to have it installed though. Ed.||||reg||1
Z||000022||Elenor84||05-29-2001||09:29 PM||||Wow!  Ed...that is a very generous offer...thank you very much...I will pour my heart into it until the end of the week...then...if nothing else I will except your offer...<P>thx again!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000023||V8Dreamer||05-29-2001||11:32 PM||||Elenor,<P>Try detaching both the shift and select cables (remember which is which) and then attempt to shift the tranny through all gears including reverse.  If you can successfully do this your problem probably lies somewhere besides the tranny, like the cables or shifter.  If you CAN shift into all of the gears manually (in the engine compartment) then try putting the alignment pin back in your shifter and tighten the cable bolts back up.<P>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000024||EdsB52||05-30-2001||03:01 AM||||Sure, let me know. Do you have someone to install it in Canada? That might be the tricky (expensive) part. Maybe a forum member lives near and has an afternoon to donate. Ed.||||reg||1
Z||000025||ROB MAC||05-30-2001||03:23 PM||||The fact that you changed 1st to reverse with an adjustment indicates you should NOT change trannys until you get the adjustment right. I know it's hard to find help from someone ( my mechanic screwed mine up when the clutch was replaced ) but don't give up.||||reg||1
