Z||000030||StuGood||05-31-2001||12:53 AM||||Sounds like you're making progress!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  FWIW, I weighed the GM FWD 4-speed transaxle (used  with a 4-cylinder engine), from a 1982 Cavalier, while it was out for clutch replacement.<P>If memory serves, and if my bathroom scale was halfway accurate, it weighed about 70 pounds.  I imagine the weight of a 1984 Fiero 4-speed transaxle is probably in that ballpark.<P>I still hope it turns out to be just the  linkage.  Not sure about how many pivot pin(s) there are supposed to be, on the lever that transforms shifter side-to-side to shift shaft in-and-out.  <BR>      ||||reg||6
Z||000031||Elenor84||05-31-2001||02:04 AM||||I just don't know what else to try u know...I've messed around with the linkage enough...but I only put in 1 drill bit when ajusting and there is quite a bit of play in the black up and down lever...still trying to make ways of that...its parked at my house right now...thinking of bringing it to a shop for there professional opinion...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000032||ROB MAC||05-31-2001||01:31 PM||||One pin goes in SIDEWAYS toward the passenger on left side of shifter. The other goes in from the TOP at the front. My book has two arrows to show the holes. Check the cable mount on the trans where they are held in place with a U shape spring clip. Make sure they are secure. Check the black plastic sleeve at the trans end of cables for any breaks. One clutch lever seemed very sloppy and I removed most of the play by adding spacer washers to the pivot pin . It goes thru the lever and is locked in place with a cotter pin. When I adjusted the cable I pushed on the LEVER to remove any play and tightened the nut on the cable end. Right hand cable 1st.||||reg||1
Z||000033||ROB MAC||05-31-2001||01:38 PM||||I am not sure if removing the play in the lever was necessary but, I did it any way and my shifting has improved. ||||reg||1
Z||000034||Elenor84||05-31-2001||02:38 PM||||I kinda neglected to say that that black sleeve was totally broken and was not attatched at the closer end of the transmission...is this really bad?  I thought it was just to protect it from wear?...thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
